<body class="bg" onload="if(typeof show_menu==='function')show_menu();"><div id="TopBanner"></div><div id="Loading" class="popup_bg"></div>
<table class="content" style="width:100%;max-width:1500px"><tr><td style="width:200px;vertical-align:top"><div id="mainMenu"></div><div id="subMenu"></div></td><td style="vertical-align:top;min-width:0"><div id="tabMenu"></div>
<div id="mcg">
  <div class="topline"><span class="eyebrow">MERLIN • IPV4 FIREWALL MANAGEMENT</span><span class="badge">0.3.1-beta · not hardware-validated</span></div>
  <h1>MerlinWRT Advanced Firewall</h1>
  <p class="muted">Choose the countries you allow. Reputation and port rules then determine which traffic may continue.</p>
  <div id="previewNotice" class="banner hidden">INTERACTIVE DEMO — synthetic data, no connection to your router. Nothing here changes a real firewall.</div>
  <div id="message" class="banner">Loading router status…</div>
  <div id="pendingBox" class="banner bad hidden"><strong>Test policy active — <span id="countdown"></span></strong><p>Check internet access and router administration. Without confirmation, the watchdog attempts rollback.</p><button id="confirm">Working correctly: confirm</button> <button id="rollback">Restore previous configuration</button></div>
  <nav class="tabs" aria-label="Section"><button data-tab="dashboard" class="active">Overview</button><button data-tab="countries">Allowed countries</button><button data-tab="ports">Ports</button><button data-tab="reputation">IP reputation</button><button data-tab="tables">IPTables</button><button data-tab="stats">Statistics</button><button data-tab="updates">Updates</button><button data-tab="system">System & recovery</button></nav>
  <section data-panel="dashboard">
    <div class="kpis"><div class="kpi"><span>Country selection</span><strong id="kCountries">—</strong><span>allowed when the country filter is enabled</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Blocked packets</span><strong id="kBlocked">—</strong><span>since the last policy rebuild</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Active connections</span><strong id="kConnections">—</strong><span>conntrack snapshot</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Available memory</span><strong id="kMemory">—</strong><span>whole router, not just this add-on</span></div></div>
    <div class="grid"><div class="card"><h2>Decision order</h2><div class="step"><strong>1. Local or special-use IPv4?</strong><br><span class="muted">Outside this add-on's public-IP checks. The existing router firewall still decides.</span></div><div class="step"><strong>2. Country in your selection?</strong><br><span class="muted">No: block. No reputation lookup is needed for rejected traffic.</span></div><div class="step"><strong>3. Listed in a reputation blocklist?</strong><br><span class="muted">Yes: block. An allowed country does not make a malicious IP safe.</span></div><div class="step"><strong>4. Blocked by a port or extra rule?</strong><br><span class="muted">Otherwise, continue to the existing Merlin/Skynet rules. No ports are opened.</span></div></div>
    <div class="card"><h2>Policy and coverage</h2><label class="check"><input id="enabled" type="checkbox">Enable Advanced Firewall</label><p id="coverage" class="muted"></p><div id="warnings"></div><div class="toolbar"><button id="refreshStatus">Refresh router status</button><button class="danger" id="disable">Disable add-on filtering</button></div><p class="small muted">Every public IPv4 packet traversing these software chains is checked locally. This is not a fresh online score for every unknown IP. Accelerated traffic and traffic bypassing the router are not automatically covered.</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section data-panel="countries" class="hidden"><div class="card"><div class="topline"><h2>Which countries do you allow?</h2><span class="badge" id="selectionCount">0 selected</span></div><label class="check"><input id="countryEnabled" type="checkbox">Allow only the selected countries</label><p class="muted">Inbound checks use the source IP; outbound checks use the destination IP. Unselected countries and addresses absent from the loaded country data are blocked.</p><div class="row"><label>Find a country<input id="countrySearch" placeholder="Netherlands, Germany or NL" autocomplete="off"></label><button id="clearCountries">Clear selection</button></div><div id="selectedChips" class="chips"></div><div id="countryList" class="country-grid"></div><div class="banner">At least one country is required to enable the country filter. Clearing the selection disables the draft filter only. The active policy changes only after testing and confirmation.</div><details><summary>Source, performance and limitations</summary><p>Source: ebrasha/cidr-ip-ranges-by-country. Only selected countries' IPv4 files are loaded, pinned to a commit. Empty or incomplete downloads never replace a valid active list.</p><p>Country allocation does not prove a user's physical location or identity. VPNs, proxies and international hosting limit country filtering. Keep required DNS, time and download services reachable.</p></details></div><div class="card">
  <h2>Country IPv4 list updates</h2>
  <p class="muted">Refresh the selected countries without downloading the complete world database. Files from an unchanged commit are reused.</p>
  <div class="row"><label class="check"><input id="countryAutoUpdate" type="checkbox">Update country lists automatically</label>
  <label>Check every (hours)<input id="countryInterval" type="number" min="1" max="720" value="24"></label></div>
  <div class="toolbar"><button id="countryUpdateSave">Save country update preferences</button><button id="countryRefresh">Update selected country lists now</button></div>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody><tr><th>Last successful country check</th><td id="countryLastSuccess">—</td></tr><tr><th>Next scheduled check</th><td id="countryNextCheck">—</td></tr><tr><th>Last refresh entry count</th><td id="countryEntries">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p class="banner" id="countryUpdateMessage"></p><p id="countryUpdateError" class="banner bad hidden"></p>
  <p class="small muted">Valid intervals: 1–720 hours. Disabling automatic updates does not disable filtering or the manual refresh button. Scheduled updates use confirmed country choices. A manual refresh of different draft choices only caches those files; it does not change your active selection. Failed downloads retain the last active policy.</p>
</div></section>
  <section data-panel="ports" class="hidden"><div class="card"><h2>Block ports</h2><p class="muted">These rules cover public internet traffic after country and reputation checks. Local cameras and other local devices remain subject to your existing firewall policy.</p><div class="row"><label>Direction<select id="portDirection"><option value="both">Inbound & outbound</option><option value="out">Outbound</option><option value="in">Inbound</option></select></label><label>Protocol<select id="portProtocol"><option value="both">TCP & UDP</option><option value="tcp">TCP</option><option value="udp">UDP</option></select></label><label>Port / range<input id="portValue" placeholder="443 or 1000-2000"></label><label>Port to match<select id="portSide"><option value="remote">Remote peer's port</option><option value="destination">Packet destination port</option><option value="either">Source or destination port</option></select></label><button id="addPort">Add rule</button></div><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Direction</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Ports</th><th>Port side</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody id="portRows"></tbody></table></div><details><summary>How are ports matched?</summary><p><strong>Remote peer:</strong> destination port outbound, source port inbound. Useful for blocking an external service and its responses.</p><p><strong>Destination:</strong> the destination port in each packet; inbound this is the public port before port forwarding.</p><p><strong>Either:</strong> a match on either source or destination blocks the packet. This can also affect an unrelated ephemeral source port with the same number.</p></details></div></section>
  <section data-panel="reputation" class="hidden"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h2>Automatic traffic checks</h2><label class="check"><input id="skynet" type="checkbox">Mirror Skynet blocklists locally</label><p class="small muted">No API call per connection. Remove conflicting country blocks from the original Skynet configuration before enabling this country allowlist.</p><label class="check"><input id="abuse" type="checkbox">Add the AbuseIPDB blocklist</label><label>Block from abuse score<input id="score" type="number" min="25" max="100" value="90"></label><p id="keyState" class="small muted"></p><details><summary>Configure the API key</summary><p>Run over SSH:</p><code>/jffs/scripts/mcg key</code><p>Input is hidden. The key is stored with permissions 0600, never in JavaScript or the public web directory.</p></details><p class="small muted">Higher scores mean more evidence of abuse. An unlisted address is unknown, not proven safe. This integration requests at most 10,000 blacklist entries. API quotas and subscription limits apply. The local threshold filters the records actually received, not the provider's entire database.</p><button id="refreshFeeds">Refresh reputation sources</button></div><div class="card"><h2>Investigate an IP address</h2><label>Public IPv4 address<input id="lookupIp" placeholder="For example 1.1.1.1"></label><div class="toolbar"><button id="lookupLocal">Check local lists</button><button id="lookupOnline">Get AbuseIPDB details</button></div><div id="lookupResult"></div><p class="small muted">Detail lookups supplement automatic filtering. Online checks are skipped when the country policy rejects the IP. A detail lookup alone does not change the rules.</p></div></div><div class="card"><h2>Loaded sources</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Source / country</th><th>Entries</th><th>Last fetched</th><th>Revision / threshold</th></tr></thead><tbody id="sourceRows"></tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section data-panel="tables" class="hidden"><div class="card"><div class="toolbar"><h2>Current IPTables</h2><div><button id="readTables">Read tables</button> <button id="exportTables">Export TXT</button></div></div><p class="muted">Read raw, mangle, nat and filter tables with counters. This full view is read-only. Edit this add-on's own validated rules below.</p><label>Filter displayed lines<input id="tableSearch" placeholder="Find DROP, MCG or port 443"></label><pre id="tablesText">Click Read tables.</pre></div><div class="card"><h2>Edit custom IPTables rules</h2><p>Validated DROP rules only, after country and reputation checks. No arbitrary shell, ACCEPT, global flush or changes to another add-on's chains.</p><label>Rules<textarea id="extraRules" spellcheck="false" placeholder="# direction + iptables match + DROP&#10;out -p tcp -d 8.8.8.8/32 --dport 853 -j DROP&#10;both -p udp --dport 1900 -j DROP"></textarea></label><p class="small muted">Up to 12 rules. Supported options: -p, -s, -d, --sport, --dport and -j DROP. Direction: in, out or both. Apply with the shared policy test button.</p></div></section>
  <section data-panel="stats" class="hidden">
  <div class="kpis"><div class="kpi"><span>Router CPU usage</span><strong id="statCpu">—</strong><span>measured between samples</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Blocked packets / second</span><strong id="statDropRate">—</strong><span>this add-on; interval average</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Local / remote IPs</span><strong id="statUnique">—</strong><span>distinct IPs in displayed snapshot</span></div><div class="kpi"><span>Conntrack utilization</span><strong id="statConntrack">—</strong><span>current kernel count / capacity</span></div></div>
  <div class="card"><h2>Sampling and retention</h2><div class="row"><label>Sample every (minutes)<input id="statsInterval" type="number" min="1" max="60" value="1"></label><label>Keep history (hours)<input id="statsRetention" type="number" min="1" max="168" value="24"></label><label>Ranking rows<input id="statsTopN" type="number" min="5" max="50" value="20"></label></div><div class="toolbar"><button id="statsSave">Save statistics preferences</button><button id="statsRefresh">Collect a sample now</button><button id="statsExport">Export statistics JSON</button></div><p id="statsSampleInfo" class="small muted"></p><p id="statsHealth" class="banner bad hidden"></p><details><summary>What these statistics can and cannot show</summary><div id="statsNotes"></div><p>Statistics sampling does not limit packet inspection. Packet filtering stays in the kernel. No packet payloads, per-connection online lookups or automatic conntrack-accounting changes are introduced.</p></details></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="toolbar"><h2>History and interface traffic</h2><button id="statsHistoryExport">Export selected history CSV</button></div><div class="row"><label>History window<select id="statsWindow"><option value="1">Last hour</option><option value="6">Last 6 hours</option><option value="24" selected>Last 24 hours</option><option value="168">Last 7 days</option></select></label><label>Metric<select id="statsMetric"><option value="cpu_percent">CPU usage (%)</option><option value="load">Load average</option><option value="blocked_pps">Blocked packets / second</option><option value="connections">Read conntrack records</option></select></label><label>Traffic interface<select id="statsInterface"></select></label></div>
  <h3 id="statsChartTitle">CPU usage (%)</h3><svg id="statsChart" class="chart" viewBox="0 0 800 130" role="img" aria-label="Selected statistics history"></svg>
  <h3>Selected interface traffic (Mbit/s)</h3><p class="small muted">Receive and transmit rates are averages between samples, not instantaneous speeds. Missing baselines are shown as gaps.</p><svg id="trafficChart" class="chart" viewBox="0 0 800 130" role="img" aria-label="Receive and transmit history"></svg>
  <h3>Router load average</h3><svg id="loadChart" class="chart" viewBox="0 0 800 130" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-label="Measured load average"></svg>
  <p class="small muted">Histories are kept in RAM with at most one USB checkpoint per hour. A reboot can lose up to one hour of recent history. Policy rebuilds reset rule counters; interval gaps are not silently treated as zero.</p></div>
  <div class="card"><h2>Network interfaces</h2><p class="small muted">Per-interface totals since their counters started. Bridged and VLAN interfaces can count the same traffic; these rows are deliberately not summed.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Interface</th><th>Receive rate</th><th>Transmit rate</th><th>Received total</th><th>Transmitted total</th></tr></thead><tbody id="interfaceRows"></tbody></table></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="toolbar"><h2>Current connection rankings</h2><label>Group by<select id="statsGroup"><option value="local_ips">Local IP address</option><option value="remote_ips">Remote IP address</option><option value="ports">Original destination port</option><option value="protocols">Protocol</option><option value="states">Connection state</option></select></label><button id="statsTopExport">Export ranking CSV</button></div><p class="small muted">Sorted by observed connections in the current capped snapshot. Known bytes belong to still-present flows and are not a period traffic total. Unknown bytes are never treated as measured zero.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Observed connections</th><th>Known flow bytes</th><th>Rows with byte counters</th></tr></thead><tbody id="rankingRows"></tbody></table></div></div>
  <div class="card"><h2>Changes since the previous sample</h2><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Direction</th><th>Decision rule</th><th>Action</th><th>Packets in interval</th><th>Bytes in interval</th><th>Packets / second</th></tr></thead><tbody id="deltaRows"></tbody></table></div></div>
  <div class="card"><div class="toolbar"><h2>Packet counters by decision rule</h2><button id="exportCounters">Export CSV</button></div><p class="muted">Packets and bytes, not counts of hackers or unique connections. Counters restart when a new policy generation is built.</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Direction</th><th>Reason</th><th>Action</th><th>Packets</th><th>Bytes</th></tr></thead><tbody id="counterRows"></tbody></table></div></div><div class="card"><div class="toolbar"><h2>Connection snapshot</h2><button id="exportConnections">Export CSV</button></div><div class="row"><label>Search IP, port or state<input id="connectionSearch" placeholder="10.10.10.10, 443, ESTABLISHED…"></label><label>Protocol<select id="connectionProto"><option value="">All protocols</option><option value="tcp">TCP</option><option value="udp">UDP</option><option value="icmp">ICMP</option></select></label><label>Direction<select id="connectionDirection"><option value="">All directions</option><option value="out">Outbound</option><option value="in">Inbound</option><option value="local">Local</option><option value="public/router">Public / router</option></select></label><label>Order<select id="connectionSort"><option value="native">Snapshot order</option><option value="bytes">Highest known byte count</option><option value="destination">Destination IP</option></select></label></div><p id="snapshotNote" class="small muted"></p><div class="tablewrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>Destination</th><th>Protocol</th><th>Source port</th><th>Destination port</th><th>State</th><th>Bytes*</th></tr></thead><tbody id="connectionRows"></tbody></table></div><p class="small muted">Up to 250 matching rows are displayed; CSV includes all collected matching rows. *Byte counts may be unavailable when conntrack accounting is disabled. Snapshots are not a complete historical audit log.</p></div></section>
  <section data-panel="updates" class="hidden"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h2>GitHub software updates</h2><p><strong>Repository:</strong> <span id="updateRepo">wootje/MerlinWRTadvancedfirewall</span><br><strong>Branch:</strong> main</p><div class="tablewrap"><table><tbody><tr><th>Installed version</th><td id="updateVersion">—</td></tr><tr><th>Installed commit</th><td id="updateInstalled">—</td></tr><tr><th>Latest checked version</th><td id="updateLatestVersion">—</td></tr><tr><th>Latest checked commit</th><td id="updateLatest">—</td></tr><tr><th>Last successful check</th><td id="updateChecked">—</td></tr><tr><th>Next scheduled check</th><td id="updateNextCheck">—</td></tr><tr><th>Downloaded package</th><td id="updateStaged">—</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p id="updateMessage" class="banner"></p><p id="updateError" class="banner bad hidden"></p><a id="updateCommitLink" class="button hidden" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Review checked commit on GitHub</a><div class="toolbar"><button id="updateCheck">Check for changes</button><button id="updateDownload">Download checked update</button><button id="updateInstall" class="primary">Install downloaded update</button></div><p class="small muted">Checks compare commit IDs, so changes are detected even when the version number is unchanged. Downloads are pinned to the checked commit. Nothing is installed automatically.</p></div><div class="card"><h2>GitHub update preferences</h2><label class="check"><input id="updateEnabled" type="checkbox">Enable GitHub software updates</label><label class="check"><input id="updateAutoCheck" type="checkbox">Check GitHub automatically</label><label class="check"><input id="updateAutoDownload" type="checkbox">Download changes automatically after checking</label><label>Check every (hours)<input id="updateInterval" type="number" min="1" max="720" value="24"></label><p class="small muted">Valid intervals: 1–720 hours. Turn off automatic checks for manual-only operation. Turn off Enable GitHub software updates to stop checks, downloads and installations; local rollback remains available. Country and reputation updates are independent.</p><button id="updateSave">Save update preferences</button><p class="small muted">Only one package is staged. A source archive is limited to 12 MiB, extracted files to 40 MiB. Checks and downloads are deferred during a firewall trial, high load, low RAM or low USB space. The browser polls local status, not GitHub.</p><h3>Installation and recovery</h3><p>Installation requires your confirmation and creates an application backup. Private configuration and API keys remain separate. Active kernel rules are not replaced by a software update.</p><p id="updateBackup" class="small muted"></p><button id="updateRollback" class="danger">Restore previous application</button><p class="small muted">Reload the page after installation. Existing firewall rules continue until a normal policy rebuild or reboot. Hashes detect corruption; they are not independent signatures and do not protect against a compromised repository account. Keep a working SSH session and a router configuration backup.</p></div></div></section>
  <section data-panel="system" class="hidden"><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h2>Preflight check</h2><p class="muted">Activation is refused until preflight passes. This package does not silently change acceleration, WAN administration or IPv6 settings.</p><pre id="doctorText">No system details yet.</pre><button id="doctor">Run preflight again</button><label>Maximum connection details<input id="maxRows" type="number" min="100" max="5000" value="3000"></label></div><div class="card"><h2>SSH recovery</h2><p>Disable this add-on without clearing the original firewall:</p><pre>/jffs/scripts/mcg disable</pre><p>If Python or USB storage is unavailable, flush only this add-on's anchors:</p><pre>/jffs/scripts/mcg emergency-off</pre><p class="small muted">The emergency marker lasts until clear-emergency or reboot. Saved settings remain. Reboot may restore the confirmed policy. Normal disable is persistent. Do not rely on this unvalidated beta as your only protection.</p><h3>Scope</h3><p class="small muted">GT-AX11000 in router mode, Merlin Addons API, Entware Python 3.9+ and IPv6 disabled. Same-switch/bridge traffic, traffic bypassing this router and the encrypted contents of tunnels are not automatically inspected.</p></div></div></section>
  <div class="sticky toolbar"><span id="dirtyLabel" class="small muted">No local changes.</span><div><button id="resetDraft">Reset draft</button> <button id="apply" class="primary">Test policy for 120 seconds</button></div></div>
  <p class="footer">Independent Skynet add-on. Not an official ASUS, Asuswrt-Merlin, Skynet or AbuseIPDB release. Source code and recovery instructions are included.</p>
</div>
</td></tr></table><div id="footer"></div><iframe name="mcg_frame" style="display:none" title="Achtergrondactie"></iframe>
